00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:45.000
But king f6 is quite unwieldy because

00:30:45.000 --> 00:30:47.000
we essentially put our king in front of our own

00:30:47.000 --> 00:30:49.000
pawns. Let's break through with f5.

00:30:49.000 --> 00:30:51.000
I think this is our chance to do it.

00:30:51.000 --> 00:30:53.000
Our opponent finding all the tricky

00:30:53.000 --> 00:30:55.000
lines here. Let's take with the g-pawn.

00:30:55.000 --> 00:30:57.000
Of course, king e5,

00:30:57.000 --> 00:30:59.000
rook d5 is checkmate, so white has to drop

00:30:59.000 --> 00:31:01.000
